  "schema_version": "numek.cg4_verification_manifest/1.0",
  "scope": "Historical positive-contamination and identity/exposure boundary. Genuine d8f73aaa captures retain typed rows without new markers and legacy CG3 binding context. Completed controls block the status-derived gate, preserve old objects and reconstruct720 exact old event/source identities; missing/ambiguous origins are not guessed. A legacy historical store lacking spec.outcomes exposed a real crash; an incorrect target-fact lookup and a fixture binding-type error were corrected, with failed records retained. Capture metadata is a transitive assessment dependency. Inline outcome use no longer bypasses tracking: shared existing authority semantics preserve serialized fields and CG1 reductions. Focused 15-test historical/status group, 11-test exposure/dependency group, a metadata dependency test, nine CG1/CG2 regressions, two focused inline checks each on3.12/3.13/3.14, and two exact key/definition references pass at their recorded source boundaries. Counts overlap. The context-only unrelated-column control was unassessed; a summary corrects its old false encoding without replay. No empirical statistical qualification, whole-history freshness guarantee, final product closure or milestone completion is asserted."
